    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A federal republic of twenty-six cantons, created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> in 1803 and turned into a federal state by the constitution of 1848.</li><li>Its permanent neutrality, recognised in 1815, kept it out of every European war since and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> a centre of diplomacy.</li><li>Referendums and popular initiatives give its citizens an unusually direct say in law-making at federal and cantonal level.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Swiss men voted on whether women should have the federal vote: they refused in 1959 and agreed only in 1971, and Appenzell Innerrhoden had to be ordered by the Federal Supreme Court to admit women in 1990.</p></aside>
    </section>

